  "description": "A quick, practical guide to Fetal Alcohol: Broken Migration.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Developing neurons must travel to precise locations in the brain.",
      "visual": "🗺️"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Alcohol disrupts these guide rails.",
      "visual": "🛤️"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "Misplaced neurons fail to form proper synapses, leaving circuits permanently miswired and reducing overall brain volume.",
      "visual": "🔗"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Alcohol also triggers massive apoptosis, programmed cell death, wiping out neurons that the developing brain cannot replace.",
      "visual": "💀"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "The damage depends on timing: first-trimester exposure disrupts migration, while third-trimester exposure disrupts synapse.",
      "visual": "📅"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "A brain under construction has no margin for error.",
      "visual": "🏗️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "How does prenatal alcohol exposure disrupt brain development?",
    "options": [
      "It derails neuron migration and triggers widespread cell death",
      "It only affects the spinal cord",
      "It accelerates brain growth beyond normal limits"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
